# dispatcher.env: tunables for the always-on work dispatcher (issue #444,
# UNIT U3 -- scripts/dispatcher-tick.sh).
#
# Format: plain KEY=VALUE lines, one per key, no inline comments after the
# value. This file is read by grepping literal "^KEY=" lines (see
# dispatcher-status.sh and dispatcher-tick.sh) -- it is deliberately NEVER
# `source`d. Sourcing an arbitrary file executes it; grepping a line just
# reads a string. An inline "# ..." comment after a value would itself
# become part of the grep-extracted value (cut -d= -f2- does not strip
# trailing comments), so keep values on their own and document meaning here
# in the header instead.
#
# Keys:
#   K              Backpressure ceiling (R6): the dispatcher will not
#                  dispatch a new run while this many or more loop-run PRs
#                  are already open org-wide. Read by dispatcher-tick.sh's
#                  BACKPRESSURE gate and mirrored read-only by
#                  dispatcher-status.sh. Default if the file or key is
#                  missing: 10.
#   YIELD_MAX      Ceiling on other live sessions (per hooks/lib/
#                  live-sessions.js --list) before the dispatcher yields
#                  the machine instead of dispatching (R-YIELD gate).
#                  Default if missing: 0 (yield to any other live session).
#   RUNG           Calibration rung/ratchet marker, recorded verbatim into
#                  each claimed ledger row's config-ratchets field
#                  (dispatcher-ledger.sh append --config-ratchets
#                  "rung=$RUNG") so a ledger read can tell which tuning
#                  generation produced a given run. Not otherwise
#                  interpreted by this unit. Default if missing: 0.
#   ORG            GitHub org the BACKPRESSURE (GraphQL search) and INTAKE
#                  (gh-ready.sh --org) gates query. Overridable per-process
#                  via the DISPATCHER_ORG env var (env wins over this
#                  file, mirroring dispatcher-status.sh's own precedent).
#                  Default if missing: StartupBros-com.
#   CADENCE_MINS   Expected minutes between ticks. Passed through to
#                  dispatcher-ledger.sh reconcile's --cadence-mins so
#                  orphaned-claim aging (a claimed row with no launched row
#                  after roughly one cadence) uses the dispatcher's actual
#                  tick interval rather than the ledger CLI's own
#                  standalone default (20). Default if missing: 15.
#   MAX_USD        Hard dollar ceiling for one dispatched claude-loop run
#                  (issue #562 amendment, operator decision 2026-08-28).
#                  dispatcher-tick.sh validates it and exports it to the
#                  launched run as CLAUDE_LOOP_MAX_USD; claude-loop.sh
#                  passes it to `claude -p --max-budget-usd`. Decimal
#                  values allowed (a dollar amount, unlike the integer
#                  keys above). Raised from the original $20 default: the
#                  first feature-sized run was killed ~90% done near $20,
#                  so the fence was eating legitimate work; $60 lets a
#                  feature finish while still catching a true runaway
#                  early. Calibration beyond that is a ratchet-doc concern
#                  fed by the ledger's budget-stopped counter, not this
#                  header. Default if missing: 60.
#   YIELD_ALLOWLIST
#                  Comma-separated list of session ids and/or pids that
#                  the YIELD gate excludes from its "other live session"
#                  count even when present (e.g. a known long-running
#                  monitoring session that should never block dispatch).
#                  Matched against both the live-sessions.js `sessionId`
#                  field and the `pid` field, as plain string membership --
#                  no globbing. Calibrated empty at rung 0; expected to
#                  gain entries only as specific false-positive yields are
#                  observed and diagnosed, never pre-emptively. Default if
#                  missing: empty (no exclusions).
#   REPO_ROOTS     Colon-separated list of candidate local checkout roots
#                  dispatcher-tick.sh's DISPATCH gate probes, in order, for
#                  the target repo's existing checkout ($root/<repo-name>/
#                  .git as either a directory -- a normal clone -- or a file
#                  -- a git worktree's gitdir pointer). The first root that
#                  has one wins and is passed to wt-new.sh as ROOT=<that
#                  root>; no match -> defer:claim-failed plus a discord
#                  alert (an operator problem: a repo was tagged loop-ok
#                  with no local checkout anywhere in this list). Real
#                  per-project repos live under $HOME/SITES; dotfiles itself
#                  lives directly under $HOME -- both need probing since
#                  either can be the target of a dispatched issue. This file
#                  is grep-parsed, not sourced (see header above), so a
#                  literal "$HOME" in the value below is NOT shell-expanded
#                  by the read -- dispatcher-tick.sh does one explicit
#                  string substitution on the extracted value afterward
#                  (never an `eval`) to resolve it against its own $HOME.
#                  Default if missing: "$HOME/SITES:$HOME".
#   PRO_GATE_INPUT_POLICY
#                  The pro-gate runtime's delivery policy for the wrapper-
#                  driven review loop (dotfiles#985, #997). bundle-only sends
#                  the PR diff as an uploaded bundle, which fails above
#                  oracle's 60,000-char inline budget (2 of 12 upload-mode
#                  attempts succeeded on 2026-09-04; pro-gate#145).
#                  connector-enabled lets a review ask ChatGPT to read the
#                  pull request through its GitHub connector instead. The
#                  connector grant itself lives on the ChatGPT side and is
#                  neither set nor verified here. Operator decision
#                  2026-09-04: connector-enabled. Default if missing:
#                  bundle-only (the runtime's own default).
#   PRO_GATE_LOOP_INPUT
#                  The delivery mode the loop passes to the runtime as
#                  --input: bundle, both, connector, auto, or empty for the
#                  runtime's default under the policy above (both when
#                  connector-enabled). connector does not inline or upload
#                  the diff at all; both still uploads it. bundle or both
#                  under bundle-only is refused by the runtime, so the tick
#                  clears an incompatible mode loudly. auto is the loop's
#                  own choice per run: both when the PR's endpoint diff is
#                  at most PRO_GATE_LOOP_INLINE_MAX_BYTES (50,000 by
#                  default) AND the size oracle would render it to fits
#                  PRO_GATE_LOOP_INLINE_BUDGET_CHARS (60,000, oracle's own
#                  inline budget) with PRO_GATE_LOOP_INLINE_RESERVE_CHARS
#                  (10,000) held back for the runtime's prompt and oracle's
#                  file framing, else connector. Rendered size is not raw
#                  size: oracle line-numbers every line it inlines, so a
#                  many-line patch overflows the budget well under the byte
#                  ceiling (dotfiles#1012 gate round 1, P1). Only a bundle-backed
#                  SHIP binds into merge proof (pro-gate#147), so both is
#                  what lets the wrapper reach a typed allow: #169 (13,493
#                  bytes) allowed in one round as both on 2026-09-05, while
#                  the connector runs on #158/#161 ended on an unbindable
#                  SHIP and better-ccflare#327 (69,521 bytes) stalled twice
#                  as an upload. Operator decision 2026-09-04: connector for
#                  dispatched loops; auto keeps that for diffs the inline
#                  path cannot carry. Default if missing: empty.
# YIELD_MAX calibration note (2026-08-28, issue #549): raised 0 -> 24 by
# operator decision ("stop counting sessions"). This box runs ~16 standing
# Claude sessions (background jobs, timers, interactive), so a session count
# cannot distinguish idle from busy here and 0 could never dispatch; the
# backpressure ceiling K stays the real throttle. Note the yield gate's
# count computation was also broken until the same date -- it errored on
# every tick and the failure printed as defer:yield, which YIELD_MAX=0 made
# look correct.
K=10
YIELD_MAX=24
RUNG=2
ORG=StartupBros-com
CADENCE_MINS=15
# Runaway fence, not a budget (operator, 2026-09-03: let dispatched runs use
# the compute they need). The #923 real-work run came in under 60 on Claude's
# own meter while spending roughly half its tokens on a self-review round
# that found three real findings; a medium issue with the same round would
# hit 60 and be cut short mid-review, which reads as a defect. 120 is twice
# the observed maximum. A run that needs more is something to read, not a
# number to raise again. (dotfiles#965)
MAX_USD=120
YIELD_ALLOWLIST=
REPO_ROOTS=$HOME/SITES:$HOME
PRO_GATE_INPUT_POLICY=connector-enabled
PRO_GATE_LOOP_INPUT=auto
